  "hook": "What happens if you stop sleeping?",
  "b1": "After twenty-four hours, your brain works like you're legally drunk.",
  "b2": "After thirty-six hours, your brain starts shutting off for seconds at a time.",
  "b3": "After forty-eight hours, stress hormones rise, and your heart beats faster.",
  "b4": "After seventy-two hours, you may start seeing things that aren't there.",
  "b5": "The record without sleep is about eleven days.",
  "end": "So, how much did you sleep last night?"
